# Prophet (forecast/prophet_source.py), the two methods that forecast the
# regular orders day by day, on top of the whole service. `make lock`
# compiles this, with the service's own pins, into requirements-prophet.txt:
# one hashed lock installed IN PLACE of requirements-service.txt.
#
# It is NOT in the nightly image. Measured on the shop's own months (October
# 2026) it was a little closer than the methods already there, by less than
# the noise, and the range drawn around it held fewer of the months that came
# in; it is about 115 MB and eleven packages, matplotlib among them, which it
# requires and never uses here. CI installs this lock to test it, and
# `python -m forecast evaluate` measures it again whenever asked. To switch it
# on: install this file in place of requirements-service.txt in
# forecast/Dockerfile, and add `python -m forecast.prophet_source` to the
# image check in .github/workflows/tests.yml, which fits it once inside the
# built image.
-r requirements-service.in
prophet==1.5.0
